# Chaperone — environment template.
# Copy to .env.local. Never commit .env.local (see .gitignore).
#
# EVERY key here is OPTIONAL. Chaperone runs fully on the keyless path
# (PROJECT-PLAN.md §10.6). A missing key makes exactly one panel render
# the "not configured" state naming the variable — nothing else breaks.
#
# These are OPERATOR keys belonging to this deployment. Chaperone never
# accepts, stores or proxies a USER's credentials for any database (§3.1).

# Identifies us to the APIs we call (§5.3), so an administrator who sees our
# traffic can find out what it is and who to tell. §10.8 is settled: the
# deployed site is the contact address, because it is public, it is stable
# across redeploys, and — unlike an email — it discloses nothing personal.
# Set in Vercel for production; set it here too if you run against the real
# APIs locally, since an unidentified client is the one most likely throttled.
#
# Use the account-NEUTRAL alias, not the long per-account deployment URL. That
# longer form embeds the Vercel account handle, and this string is sent to all
# eighteen third-party APIs on every request — the contact address should
# identify the TOOL, never its operator.
CHAPERONE_CONTACT_URL=https://chaperone-cyan.vercel.app

# NCBI E-utilities (ClinVar, dbSNP, NCBI Virus).
# Keyless works at 3 req/s; a free key raises it to 10 req/s.
# https://account.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/settings/
NCBI_API_KEY=

# OMIM. Free academic key, issued per person.
# https://www.omim.org/api
OMIM_API_KEY=

# BioGRID / BioGRID ORCS. Free self-service key.
# https://webservice.thebiogrid.org/
BIOGRID_API_KEY=

# Synapse (PsychENCODE). Free account + personal access token.
# https://www.synapse.org/
SYNAPSE_TOKEN=
